{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "7c1f4a52-9d3e-4b8a-a6c1-2f0b5e9d4a11",
    "name": "Users API",
    "description": "User management module: registration, JWT authentication, email/SMS verification, role-based access control and user administration.\n\n## Getting started\n\n1. Start the stack: `docker compose up --build -d`\n2. Check `baseUrl` below matches your published port (default `http://localhost:8000`).\n3. Run the requests top to bottom — tokens and identifiers are captured into collection variables automatically, so nothing has to be copied by hand.\n\n## The one manual step\n\nVerification codes are not emailed in development; they are written to the application log. Before running **Verify account**, read the code from:\n\n```\ndocker compose logs --tail 50 api\n```\n\nand paste it into the `verificationCode` collection variable.\n\nEvery other request in the collection is fully automated and carries assertions, so `Run collection` doubles as a smoke test of a deployment.\n\n## Credentials\n\nThe administrator is created on first startup from `FIRST_ADMIN_EMAIL` / `FIRST_ADMIN_PASSWORD` (`admin@example.com` / `Admin12345` in `.env.example`). Regular users are registered with a unique address generated per run.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminEmail", "value": "admin@example.com", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminPassword", "value": "Admin12345", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "userEmail", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "userPassword", "value": "Str0ngPassw0rd", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "verificationCode", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminAccessToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "createdUserId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "profilePhone", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Probes used by orchestrators. Neither requires authentication.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["health"] },
            "description": "Returns 200 as long as the process is running."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('reports ok', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('ok'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/ready",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health", "ready"]
            },
            "description": "Verifies that the database is reachable before accepting traffic."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('database reachable', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Authentication",
      "description": "Registration, verification, login, token rotation and logout.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sign up",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\",\n  \"first_name\": \"Ada\",\n  \"last_name\": \"Lovelace\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/signup",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "signup"]
            },
            "description": "Registers a user. The email must be unique. The account starts **unverified** and a one-time code is sent through the configured channel — in development it is written to the application log. Unverified accounts are deleted automatically after two days."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// A fresh address per run keeps the collection re-runnable.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userEmail', `ada.${Date.now()}@example.com`);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userPassword', 'Str0ngPassw0rd');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('starts unverified', () => pm.expect(body.user.is_verified).to.eql(false));",
                  "pm.test('default role is user', () => pm.expect(body.user.role).to.eql('user'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', body.user.id);",
                  "console.log('Registered ' + body.user.email);",
                  "console.log('Read the code with: docker compose logs --tail 50 api');",
                  "console.log('then paste it into the verificationCode variable.');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify account",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"code\": \"{{verificationCode}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/verify",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "verify"]
            },
            "description": "Confirms the one-time code and marks the account as **verified**.\n\nSet `verificationCode` first — read it from `docker compose logs --tail 50 api`.\n\nCodes are single-use, expire after 15 minutes and lock after five failed attempts."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('verificationCode')) {",
                  "    console.warn('verificationCode is empty — read it from the API log first.');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('account is verified', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().is_verified).to.eql(true));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Resend verification code",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/verify/resend",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "verify", "resend"]
            },
            "description": "Issues a new code and invalidates the previous one. The response is identical whether or not the address is registered, so the endpoint cannot be used to enumerate accounts."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Exchanges credentials for a short-lived access token and a long-lived refresh token. Both are stored into collection variables by the test script."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('bearer token pair returned', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.token_type).to.eql('bearer');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.refresh_token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.access_token);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', body.refresh_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in as administrator",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Signs in the bootstrap administrator created on first startup. Its access token is stored separately as `adminAccessToken` and used by the requests in the **Users (admin)** folder."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('adminAccessToken', pm.response.json().access_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh tokens",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refresh_token\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Exchanges a refresh token for a new pair. Refresh tokens are **single-use**: the presented token is revoked and replaced. Presenting an already-rotated token is treated as a compromise and revokes every session of that user, so sending this request twice with the same value is expected to fail the second time."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('refresh token was rotated', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.refresh_token).to.not.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('refreshToken'));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.access_token);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', body.refresh_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log out",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refresh_token\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "logout"]
            },
            "description": "Revokes the supplied refresh token. The matching access token stays valid until it expires, which is fifteen minutes by default."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log out everywhere",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout/all",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "logout", "all"]
            },
            "description": "Revokes every refresh token issued to the authenticated user."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Profile",
      "description": "Endpoints acting on the authenticated user. They use the collection-level bearer auth, which reads `accessToken`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get current user",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me"] },
            "description": "Returns the profile of the account the access token belongs to."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('no password material is exposed', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.include('hashed_password');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Update current user",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"first_name\": \"Augusta\",\n  \"phone\": \"{{profilePhone}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me"] },
            "description": "Partially updates the caller's own profile: only the fields present in the body are changed. Privileged fields (`email`, `role`, `is_active`, `is_verified`) are reserved for administrators and are rejected here.\n\nThe phone number is generated per run: it is unique across accounts, so a fixed value would collide with 409 on a database that already holds it."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Phone numbers are unique per account, so keep this run's value distinct.",
                  "const suffix = String(Date.now()).slice(-7);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('profilePhone', `+1415${suffix}`);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('change applied', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().first_name).to.eql('Augusta'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Change password",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"current_password\": \"{{userPassword}}\",\n  \"new_password\": \"NewStr0ngPass\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/password",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["me", "password"]
            },
            "description": "Replaces the caller's password after re-checking the current one. Existing sessions are left untouched; call **Log out everywhere** to revoke them.\n\nThe test script updates `userPassword`, so a later **Log in** still works."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "// Keep the variable in step so re-running Log in still succeeds.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userPassword', 'NewStr0ngPass');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Users (admin)",
      "description": "User administration. These requests authenticate with `adminAccessToken`, so run **Log in as administrator** first. A regular user's token gets 403 here.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List users",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminAccessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users?limit=50&offset=0",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "limit", "value": "50", "description": "Maximum items to return (1-200)" },
                { "key": "offset", "value": "0", "description": "Number of items to skip" },
                {
                  "key": "search",
                  "value": "ada",
                  "description": "Case-insensitive match on email or name",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "role",
                  "value": "admin",
                  "description": "Filter by role: user | admin",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "is_verified",
                  "value": "true",
                  "description": "Filter by verification status",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "is_active",
                  "value": "true",
                  "description": "Filter by activity status",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns a paginated list of users, newest first. **Admin only.** Enable the disabled query parameters to filter or search."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('paginated envelope', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.all.keys('items', 'total', 'limit', 'offset');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create user",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminAccessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{createdUserEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"Str0ngPassw0rd\",\n  \"first_name\": \"Grace\",\n  \"last_name\": \"Hopper\",\n  \"role\": \"user\",\n  \"is_verified\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["users"] },
            "description": "Creates a user with an explicit role, optionally already verified — useful for seeding. **Admin only.** Self-service registration goes through `/auth/signup`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('createdUserEmail', `grace.${Date.now()}@example.com`);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('created already verified', () => pm.expect(body.is_verified).to.eql(true));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('createdUserId', body.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get user by ID",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminAccessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{createdUserId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{createdUserId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Returns a single user by identifier. **Admin only.** Responds 404 for an unknown id and 422 for a malformed UUID."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Update user",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminAccessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"first_name\": \"Rear Admiral\",\n  \"role\": \"admin\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{createdUserId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{createdUserId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Partially updates a user. Regular users may only update their own profile and cannot change `email`, `role`, `is_active` or `is_verified`; administrators may change any field on any account.\n\nTwo lockout guards apply: an administrator may not demote or delete their own account (409)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('role changed', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().role).to.eql('admin'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete user",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminAccessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
            },
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{createdUserId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{createdUserId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Permanently deletes a user together with their verification codes and sessions. **Admin only**, and administrators cannot delete their own account."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('204 No Content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Access control checks",
      "description": "Negative cases worth seeing explicitly: they demonstrate the role and authentication boundaries rather than the happy path.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List users as a regular user (403)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["users"] },
            "description": "The same endpoint as **List users**, but authenticated with the regular user's token. Expected to be rejected with `permission_denied`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403 Forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('permission_denied', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('permission_denied');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get current user without a token (401)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me"] },
            "description": "Unauthenticated access to a protected endpoint returns the uniform error body with `invalid_token`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('uniform error body', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.all.keys('error', 'message', 'details');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Escalate own role (403)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"role\": \"admin\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["users", "{{userId}}"]
            },
            "description": "A regular user editing their own record cannot grant themselves the admin role: privileged fields are enforced in the service layer, not only in the router."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('403 Forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register a duplicate email (409)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"Str0ngPassw0rd\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/signup",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "signup"]
            },
            "description": "Email uniqueness is case-insensitive and backed by a unique index, so a race between two concurrent signups still yields exactly one account."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test('email_already_registered', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('email_already_registered');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in with a wrong password (401)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"definitely-wrong-1\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "A wrong password and an unknown address return byte-identical responses, and the unknown-address path still hashes a dummy value so the two take comparable time. Neither can be used to discover which addresses are registered."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('invalid_credentials', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('invalid_credentials');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
